+    // USM patch 0012 (screen-no-activate): never let the output window hold foreground
+    // focus.
+    //
+    // WHY. NVIDIA's driver promotes a FOCUSED, undecorated window that exactly covers
+    // a monitor to exclusive-fullscreen-style scanout ("Hardware: Legacy Flip" in
+    // PresentMon) on the first SwapBuffers — the window takes ownership of the display
+    // and DWM is switched off on that head. The operator's first click into the UI
+    // then forces a demotion back to DWM composition: a scanout teardown the monitor
+    // sees as a mode change (the first-click blink), and which some display chains
+    // (LED processors behind converters) fail to resync from — the head stays black,
+    // desktop included, until something forces a fresh modeset. A window that has
+    // NEVER been focused is never promoted, so neither transition can occur.
+    // Steady-state cost: none — after the operator's first click the classic window
+    // runs DWM-composed either way; this only removes the transition. The flip path
+    // (patch 0008) never had the problem (DWM keeps display ownership) but gets the
+    // same guard: its window is created focused too, and its one pre-flip_init
+    // SwapBuffers plus the mid-run flip->classic fallback both present on this HWND.
+    //
+    // <no-activate> in config; NOACTIVATE AMCP token so an app-side consumer recovery
+    // (ADD ... SCREEN) re-creates the window with the same guarantee instead of
+    // stealing foreground mid-show (which the pre-0012 recovery did).
+    bool            no_activate = false;
